@@ -0,0 +1,96 @@
+# Transcript Saver + Batch Auto-Transcripts — New Feature
+
+Two additions that make lecture transcripts permanent and automatic:
+
+1. **Transcript Saver** — a new section on the Download page where transcripts are
+   stored **forever** (in the app's SQLite database). They survive video deletion,
+   cache clears and page reloads — you never need to re-paste a YouTube link or
+   re-fetch captions again.
+2. **Auto-transcripts in playlist batch downloads** — in the "Download a Range from
+   a Playlist" panel you can tick **"Also fetch YouTube auto transcript for each
+   video (saved to Transcript Saver)"**. While the videos download, the backend
+   fetches each video's YouTube auto transcript **in parallel** (up to 3 at a time)
+   and saves it into the Transcript Saver automatically.
+
+---
+
+## How to use it
+
+### Transcript Saver (Download page)
+- **Paste a transcript:** type a title (e.g. "Lecture 4 – Calculus"), optionally a
+  YouTube link, paste the text, click **Save transcript**.
+- **Fetch from YouTube:** paste any YouTube link in the "or fetch from YouTube" box
+  and click **Fetch & save** — captions are fetched and saved in one click.
+- **Save any fetched transcript:** in the existing **URL Transcript** panel, after
+  fetching a transcript click **Save to Saver**.
+- **Manage:** every saved transcript has **Copy**, **Edit** (pencil) and **Delete**
+  (trash) buttons. Expand with the arrow to read the full text.
+- **Clear all:** the **Clear all** button (click twice to confirm) empties the whole
+  saver. Deleting a video or reloading the page never removes these transcripts.
+
+> Tip: pasting a YouTube link with the transcript auto-detects the video id, so
+> re-saving the same lecture updates that row instead of duplicating it.
+
+### Playlist batch downloads
+1. In **"Download a Range from a Playlist"**, paste the playlist link and pick your
+   range / specific videos (as before).
+2. Tick **"Also fetch YouTube auto transcript for each video"**.
+3. Click **Download N videos**.
+4. Downloads and transcript fetches run **at the same time**. Each video row in the
+   progress card shows a transcript flag:
+   - **Transcript saved** (green) — available and stored in the Transcript Saver
+   - **No transcript** — YouTube has no captions for that video
+   - **Fetching transcript… / Transcript queued** — in progress
+   - **Transcript error** — something went wrong (hover for details)
+5. The header shows live counts, e.g. `2/5 transcripts saved`.
+
+---
+
+## New backend endpoints
+
+| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
+| ------ | -------- | ------- |
+| GET    | `/api/transcript-saver` | List all saved transcripts |
+| POST   | `/api/transcript-saver` | Save a pasted transcript (upserts by video id/url) |
+| POST   | `/api/transcript-saver/fetch` | Fetch a YouTube auto transcript and save it |
+| GET    | `/api/transcript-saver/{id}` | Get one transcript |
+| PATCH  | `/api/transcript-saver/{id}` | Update title/text/url |
+| DELETE | `/api/transcript-saver/{id}` | Delete one transcript |
+| DELETE | `/api/transcript-saver` | **Clear all** transcripts |
+
+`POST /api/playlist/download` now also accepts `"fetch_transcripts": true`.
+
+Saved transcripts live in the SQLite table `saved_transcripts`
+(`video_id, title, url, text, source, created_at, updated_at`).
+
+---
+
+## Files changed (this feature only)
+
+**Backend**
+- `backend/routes/transcript_saver.py` *(new)* — Transcript Saver API.
+- `backend/services/database.py` — `saved_transcripts` table + CRUD functions.
+- `backend/services/playlist_batch.py` — parallel transcript fetching for batches.
+- `backend/routes/playlist_batch.py` — passes `fetch_transcripts` through.
+- `backend/models.py` — new request models + `fetch_transcripts` field.
+- `backend/main.py` — registers the new router.
+
+**Frontend**
+- `frontend/src/App.jsx` — Transcript Saver panel, batch transcript checkbox +
+  per-video transcript flags, "Save to Saver" button in the URL Transcript panel.
+- `frontend/src/App.css` — styles for the saver and transcript flags.
+
+**Docs**
+- `TRANSCRIPT_SAVER_FEATURE.md` *(this file)*.
+
+---
+
+## Notes
+- This feature is an **add-on to the playlist batch feature** (v1). Apply the v1
+  patch first, then this one.
+- Transcript text is stored in the DB, so it is independent of the downloads folder
+  and survives `Clear library`, video deletion and app restarts.
+- Transcript fetching is capped at 3 concurrent requests so a big batch won't hammer
+  YouTube; downloads are unaffected (separate queue).
+- If a video has no YouTube captions, the row shows **No transcript** — you can still
+  paste one manually into the saver.
